module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulExtComputation
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.StrictlyPerfect.StrictlyPerfectHomQuasiIso
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient into the structure sheaf

Let `Y` be a ringed space, let `ℐ ⊂ O_Y` be a sheaf of ideals and set `O_X = O_Y/ℐ`. Writing
`𝒩 = 𝓗om_{O_Y}(ℐ/ℐ², O_X)` for the normal sheaf, [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ] asserts that for `ℐ`
Koszul-regular

`R𝓗om_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) = ⋀^r 𝒩 [-r]`,

where `r` sends a point of `Y` to the minimal number of generators of `ℐ` near it. Equivalently,
the Ext sheaves `𝓔xt^i_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y)` vanish for `i ≠ r` and the `r`-th one is `⋀^r 𝒩`.

This file treats the coefficients `O_Y` — the structure sheaf itself, rather than the quotient —
in the Koszul computation of those Ext sheaves, and proves the part of the vanishing assertion
that the Koszul complex gives with no computation of its differential: **the Ext sheaves into
`O_Y` vanish in every degree outside `0, …, r`.**

The argument. For an ideal sheaf generated by a Koszul-regular sequence of `r` global sections,
the Koszul complex is a strictly perfect resolution of `O_X`, so
`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain` computes
`𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, M)` as the `n`-th cohomology sheaf of the internal Hom complex
`𝓗om^•(⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ), M)` for *every* complex `M` of coefficients; taking `M` concentrated in
degree zero on `O_Y` gives the complex whose cohomology sheaves are the Ext sheaves of the tag.
A term of a Hom complex into a complex concentrated in degree zero has exactly one nonvanishing
component, `𝓗om(⋀ⁿ((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y)` in degree `n`, and the exterior powers of a free sheaf of rank
`r` vanish in negative degrees and above `r`. So the Hom complex vanishes outside the degrees
`0, …, r`, and a cohomology sheaf in a degree where a complex vanishes is zero.

Unlike the self-Ext case of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulExtComputation`,
the Hom complex into `O_Y` does **not** have vanishing differential — on the degree-one
generators it is multiplication by the sequence — so its cohomology inside the degrees `0, …, r`
is not read off from its terms, and nothing is claimed about it here.

## What is carried

The tag's hypothesis is that `ℐ` be Koszul-regular, which is a *local* condition. What is
assumed instead, and named in the tag's clause, is a **global** Koszul presentation: a
`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData` for a morphism `φ : (O_Y)ʳ ⟶ O_Y`, with `ℐ` its image
and `O_X` the quotient, whose augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism. That is the hypothesis after
the opening reduction of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ], "we may assume that we have global
sections `f₁, …, f_r` of `O_Y` which generate `ℐ` and which form a Koszul regular sequence"; the
reduction itself is not performed, exactly as recorded for the neighbouring tag in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulSelfExtIteratedContractionStalk`. With a
global presentation the function `r` of the tag is the constant `r`.

## Deviation from the source

The source states the conclusion as a single equality in the derived category. What is proved
here is a strictly weaker statement: one half of the vanishing `𝓔xt^i = 0` for `i ≠ r`, namely
the degrees `i < 0` and `i > r`. The degrees `0, …, r - 1`, the identification of `𝓔xt^r` with
`⋀^r 𝒩`, and the derived-category isomorphism itself are **not** proved; they need the
self-duality of the Koszul complex, `𝓗om^•(⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y) ≅ ⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ)[-r]`, which
this library does not have. The clause string on the tagged theorem records the restriction.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.unitSingleComplex`: the coefficients `O_Y` of the
  tag, as a complex concentrated in degree zero.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.structureSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain`: the Ext sheaves
  `𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y)` as the cohomology sheaves of `𝓗om^•(⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y)`, which is
  the step of the proof of the tag supplied by [Stacks, Tag 08DM].

## Main results

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.isZero_sheafHomComplex_unit_X_of_notMem_Icc`: the Hom
  complex into `O_Y` vanishes in every degree outside `0, …, r`.
* `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc`: **the Ext
  sheaves of `O_X` into `O_Y` vanish in every degree outside `0, …, r`.**

## Implementation notes

The degree hypothesis is phrased as the disjunction `n < 0 ∨ (r : ℤ) < n` rather than as
`n ∉ Set.Icc 0 (r : ℤ)`, so that the two cases are available to `rcases` without unfolding set
membership; the two are equivalent by `Set.mem_Icc` and `omega`.

The term of the Koszul cochain complex in degree `-n` is the term of the Koszul chain complex in
degree `-(-n)`, definitionally and not syntactically, because `Stacks.ChainComplex.asCochain` is
a restriction along an embedding of complex shapes. The double negation is removed by
`neg_neg` after a `change`, which elaborates at default transparency; this is the same transport
that `Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.extIsoInternalHom` carries in the self-Ext case.

The conclusion is stated on `Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafExt`, which is by definition the
cohomology sheaf of the derived internal Hom of [Stacks, Tag 0BQP]. So the main result is
literally a statement about the object `R𝓗om_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y)` that the tag computes: its
cohomology sheaves vanish outside the degrees `0, …, r`. No separate derived-category
reformulation is needed.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DM)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex

universe u

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

open Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.ChainComplex

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (Rc : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat.{u} X)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology X).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {r : ℕ}
  {A : SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
    (koszulFreeSheaf Rc r)}
  {φ : koszulFreeSheaf Rc r ⟶
    SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)}

/-- **The coefficients `O_Y` of [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ]**: the structure sheaf, as a module over
itself, read as a complex concentrated in degree zero. These are the coefficients of the Ext
sheaves of the tag, in contrast with the quotient `O_X` which carries its self-Ext sheaves. -/
abbrev unitSingleComplex : CochainComplex (StructureSheafModules Rc) ℤ :=
  (single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
    (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc))

/-- **The Ext sheaves of `O_X` into `O_Y` are the cohomology sheaves of the Hom complex out of
the Koszul complex.** For `φ` whose Koszul complex resolves the quotient `O_X = O_Y/ℐ`, and for
every `n`, the Ext sheaf `𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y)` is the `n`-th cohomology sheaf of the internal
Hom complex `𝓗om^•(⋀^{-•}((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y)`.

This is the step of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ] supplied by [Stacks, Tag 08DM]: the Koszul
complex is a strictly perfect resolution of `O_X`, so the derived internal Hom out of it needs
no injective resolution of the coefficients. It is
`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain` at the coefficients
`O_Y`, which that computation accepts because it imposes no condition whatever on them. -/
def structureSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    [QuasiIso K.augmentation] (n : ℤ) :
    derivedSheafExt Rc
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
          ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
            (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (unitSingleComplex Rc)) n ≅
      (RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
        (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.homology n :=
  derivedSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain Rc K (unitSingleComplex Rc) n

/-- **The Hom complex of the Koszul complex into `O_Y` vanishes outside the degrees `0, …, r`.**
Its degree-`n` term is `𝓗om(⋀ⁿ((O_Y)ʳ), O_Y)`, the single nonvanishing component of a term of a
Hom complex into a complex concentrated in degree zero, and the exterior powers of a free sheaf
of rank `r` vanish in negative degrees and above `r`. -/
theorem isZero_sheafHomComplex_unit_X_of_notMem_Icc (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ) {n : ℤ}
    (hn : n < 0 ∨ (r : ℤ) < n) :
    IsZero ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
      (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.X n) := by
  refine IsZero.of_iso ?_ (RingedSite.homDegreeIsoSingle (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K)
    (SheafOfModules.unit (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Rc)) n)
  refine RingedSite.internalHomSheaf_isZero_of_isZero (ringedSite Rc) ?_
  show IsZero (K.chain.X (-(-n)))
  rw [neg_neg]
  rcases hn with hn | hn
  · exact K.isZero_chain_X_of_neg hn
  · refine IsZero.of_iso (RingedSite.isZero_exteriorPiece_of_card_lt (ringedSite Rc) A
      (ULift.{u} (Fin r)) (Iso.refl _) n ?_) (eqToIso (K.chain_X n))
    simpa using hn

/-- **The Ext sheaves of a Koszul-regular quotient into the structure sheaf vanish outside the
degrees `0, …, r`.** For an ideal sheaf `ℐ ⊂ O_Y` generated by a Koszul-regular sequence of `r`
global sections, with quotient `O_X = O_Y/ℐ`,

`𝓔xt^n_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) = 0` for `n < 0` and for `n > r`.

This is part of the vanishing half of [Stacks, Tag 0BQZ], whose conclusion
`R𝓗om_{O_Y}(O_X, O_Y) = ⋀^r 𝒩 [-r]` says that these Ext sheaves vanish in every degree other
than `r` and that the `r`-th one is the top exterior power of the normal sheaf. The degrees
`0, …, r - 1` and the degree `r` itself are not treated: they are where the differential of the
Hom complex, which is not zero, has to be computed. -/
@[stacks 0BQZ "ONLY the degrees outside `0, …, r` of the vanishing half of the tag: the Ext \
sheaves `Ext^i_{O_Y}(O_Y/I, O_Y)` are zero for `i < 0` and for `i > r`. Carried: the ideal \
sheaf is presented GLOBALLY by a Koszul-regular sequence of `r` sections -- a Koszul chain \
datum for `φ : (O_Y)^r ⟶ O_Y` whose augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism -- where the tag \
assumes only the local condition that `I` be Koszul-regular, so the opening reduction of its \
proof is not performed and the tag's locally varying `r` is here constant. NOT covered: the \
degrees `0, …, r - 1`, the identification of `Ext^r` with the top exterior power of the normal \
sheaf, and the derived-category isomorphism `RHom(O_X, O_Y) = (top exterior power of N)[-r]`"]
theorem isZero_derivedSheafExt_unit_of_notMem_Icc (K : KoszulChainData.{u, u, u} A φ)
    [QuasiIso K.augmentation] {n : ℤ} (hn : n < 0 ∨ (r : ℤ) < n) :
    IsZero (derivedSheafExt Rc
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        ((single (StructureSheafModules Rc) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
          (quotient Rc (φ := φ))))
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (unitSingleComplex Rc)) n) :=
  IsZero.of_iso
    (ShortComplex.isZero_homology_of_isZero_X₂
      ((RingedSite.sheafHomComplex (ringedSite Rc) (cochain Rc K) (unitSingleComplex Rc)).obj.sc n)
      (isZero_sheafHomComplex_unit_X_of_notMem_Icc Rc K hn))
    (structureSheafExtIsoHomologyCochain Rc K n)

end Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData

end
